(“FoonYue”,”Sales”,6660),(“George”,”Sales”,10563),(“Loui”,”SCM”,10449),(“Gerand’,”SRM”,6949),
(“Pamela”,”SCM”,11503),(“Larry Bott”,”SCM”,11798),(“Barry Jones”,”SCM”10586)).
scala>val df = data.toDF(“Name”,”Dept”,”Salary”)
scala> df.show()
a) Sum
1. Total sum of the salary
scala> df.agg(sum(“salary”).alias(“Total_salary”).show()
2. Sum of the particular dep salary
scala> df.groupby(“department”).sum(“salary’).show()
b) Min and Max
1. Min and Max for whole dataset
scala> df.agg(min(“salary”).alias(“min_salary”),|max(“salary’).alias(“max_sales”)).show()
2. Min and Max for the particular department
scala>df.groupBy(“department”).agg(min(“salary”).|as(“min_salary”),max(“salary”).as(“max_salary”)).
|show()
c) Average
1. Total Average
scala> df.agg(avg(“salary”).alias(‘average_salary”)).show()
2. Average for the particular department
scala> df.groupBy(“department”).avg(“salary’).show()
d) Count
1. Total count
scala> df.agg(count(“name”).alias(“employee_count”)).show()
2. Count the department
scala> df.groupBy(“department’).count().show()
